      "writtenOn": "2020-12-09T01:31:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this is a confusing concept. a couple questions:\n1) can we just igore READY and IMSI and wait for LOADED before do the retry?\n2) what about ABSENT case? we never do DDS retry if a slot is empty?\n3) what about eSIM empty profile? we had a lot of issues around this usecase and it\u0027s not taken into consideration here.\n4) what about pin locked?\nthen it\u0027s back to my original question: why SIM state transition impacts dds switch? seems to me they are different concepts. if we really want to optimization, i suggest we return false only for certain states, e.g. NOT_READY (then you still need to check eSIM empty profile). if it\u0027s too complicated, do we really want this optimization in the first place?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 475,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 477,
        "endChar": 85
      },
      "revId": "e60c3f1a5b8c40b05ce2f67c54e64fbdeb5f1cea",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ab2dbab0_31447898",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/PhoneSwitcher.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 477,
